# =============================================================================
# RESOURCE STORAGE POLICY (LOCKED — owner 2026-07-09)
# All downloaded learning resources are LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ASSETS ONLY.
# Never commit copyrighted source documents (NCERT, JEE, NEET, AIPMT, AIIMS,
# NTA samples, DPPs, question banks, mock tests, formula sheets, etc.).
# Policy: docs/curriculum-intelligence/RESOURCE_STORAGE_POLICY.md
# =============================================================================

# --- Raw resource trees (NEVER commit) ----------------------------------------
resources/
resources/foundation/
resources/archive/
resources/curriculum/
downloads/
cache/
temp/
archives/

# --- Downloaded / copyrighted binary formats (NEVER commit) ---------------------
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.epub
*.zip
*.ecar
*.rar
*.7z

# --- Acquisition runtime logs (local download traces) ---------------------------
acquisition/*.log
acquisition/*.out
acquisition/.counters.json
acquisition/.acquire.pid
acquisition/.fetch_direct.pid
# Runtime engineering logs are seeded on disk (Part-04 logs/) but are
# machine-local artifacts — keep them out of git; the tracked logs/.gitkeep
# preserves the directory.
logs/*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Knowledge Intelligence Engine local virtualenv (NEVER commit) --------------
# Dedicated Python 3.13 venv for the KIE data-lane (pypdf/PyMuPDF/pdfplumber/OCR).
# Reproducible from scripts/intelligence/requirements.txt — the env itself is local.
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Owner local-storage lock (2026-07-08) --------------------------------
# Derived / AI-generated knowledge is LOCAL ONLY — NOT committed until the
# repository-scale decision. Commit only schemas / engine / manifests / tests /
# code. PROVENANCE_MANIFEST.json (sha256 + source-URL provenance) is the ONE
# committed manifest; the parsed blueprints, populated indexes/metadata/reports,
# and acquisition state stay on local disk.
# NOTE: anchored to the DATA dir (curriculum/knowledge/) only. The unanchored
# form "knowledge/" also swallowed the ENGINE code dir
# curriculum/scripts/intelligence/kie/qie/knowledge/ — which per the rule above
# ("commit only schemas / engine / … / code") MUST be committed. Keep this anchored.
/knowledge/
indexes/*.json
metadata/resources/
reports/*.md
DOWNLOAD_QUEUE.json
COMPLETED_DOWNLOADS.json
FAILED_DOWNLOADS.json
PROJECT_STATUS.json
SESSION_LOG.md

# Crawler runtime frontier state (local-only; manifest committed separately once the real crawl runs)
acquisition/crawler_state.json

# --- Derived acquisition / discovery / reporting artifacts (LOCAL ONLY per owner lock 2026-07-08) ---
# Regenerable outputs of the acquisition/discovery/report scripts. The rules above anchored
# reports/*.md + indexes/*.json but let the derived *.json reports/catalogues + dated checkpoints
# leak through as UNTRACKED working-tree noise (added 2026-07-20, Repository Hygiene review).
# Already-tracked governed outputs (reports/CANONICAL_CURRICULUM_MATRIX.json,
# reports/OFFICIAL_UNIVERSE_RECONCILIATION.json, discovery/official_universe.json,
# reports/qp_audit/*.json) stay tracked — gitignore never untracks a committed file.
# acquisition/*MANIFEST.json is intentionally specific, NOT a blanket acquisition/*.json, so the
# future committed crawler_manifest.json (see note above) is not accidentally excluded.
reports/*.json
discovery/**/*.json
acquisition/AGENT_MANIFEST.json
acquisition/WAVE_*.json
acquisition/CHECKPOINT_*.md

# --- Non-certified question-corpus staging lane (LOCAL ONLY; overnight extraction) ---
# RAW DOCUMENT -> LOSS-MINIMISING EXTRACTION -> STRUCTURED STAGING CORPUS. Never certified,
# never production, never merged into kie.db / Certified Question Bank. Manifests+assets are
# derived local artifacts (can be gigabytes). Leading slash anchors to curriculum/staging/ ONLY
# so the harness code under curriculum/scripts/staging/ stays committable.
/staging/
